WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:08.023
A gradual rollout lets you check a small batch before expanding.
We’ll prepare a plan and leave it paused until reporting is
ready.

2
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.085
Choose Rollouts to plan a release in stages.

3
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.663
Create a gradual rollout. Choose the release and the matching
device platform.

4
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:22.925
A cohort is simply a batch. Add devices or groups; a device
belongs to only one batch.

5
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:29.802
Choose the pacing, observation period and failure threshold.
Creating the plan does not start devices.

6
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:35.487
Select the rollout. Check current device health before allowing
the first devices to start.

7
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:41.615
Devices are still waiting in this example. Current reporting
must be available before admission.

8
00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:49.293
Pause stops new admissions. It does not undo an update already
allowed to start; this example admits no devices.

9
00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:55.245
The plan is paused. Return when reporting is ready and
explicitly approve further progress.

10
00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:02.442
This plan is saved and paused, with devices still waiting. Check
current reporting before approving the next step.
